data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":2,"delta":{"type":"input_json_delta","partial_json":"{\"kind\": \"decision\", \"title\": \"Choose where to store carts: Redis or Postgres\", \"body\": \"Carts currently live in a 4 KB session cookie, and long carts get truncated. Both options move the cart server-side and keep only a session ID in the cookie.\\n\\n- Postgres: durable, transactional, queryable with orders, no new infrastructure. Needs a cleanup job for stale carts.\\n- Redis: fast, TTL expiry built in. Adds a service to run, needs persistence and memory limits set, and is harder to query for analytics.\\n\\nRecommendation: Postgres. A lost cart is lost revenue, and cart traffic is modest.\", \"actions\": [{\"label\":\"Use Postgres (Recommended)\",\"kind\":\"resolve\"},{\"label\":\"Use Redis\",\"kind\":\"resolve\"}]}"}}

